# The push cannot settle the exclusive rule, because it spans tasks: two runs
# reading an idle queue both push different refs and both succeed. So the claim
# is verified after the ref lands, and a run that finds its claim beside one it
# may not stand with deletes its own ref and reports the claim lost.
run claim M2-01
exit 4
claims M1-01
after M1-01
file tasks/M1-01.md
	---
	id: M1-01
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: no
	---
file tasks/M2-01.md
	---
	id: M2-01
	depends_on: []
	exclusive: yes
	---
stderr
	tasks.sh: claim on M2-01 released: M2-01 is exclusive and 1 other claims are in flight
